-*Run the [planning helper](../using-theseus/scripts/planning.py) with one JSON object on stdin. Set `root` to the main vault for First implementation or Modification, or to the verified prepared worktree for Refactoring or a dependent Bug fix. Pass `decision` from the router, selected `ticket` text, `plan_path` for a new plan, exact implementation `files`, and `sections` mapping exact note paths to arrays of heading paths. For example, a heading path is `["Specification", "Acceptance"]`. Pass the effective role `settings` and relevant `context`. The helper requests a read-only planner proposal and checks and writes the resulting documents.*
+*For Refactoring, use the [confirmed refactoring procedure](../using-git-worktrees/SKILL.md) to prepare or resume planning. For other work, run the [planning helper](../using-theseus/scripts/planning.py) with one JSON object on stdin. Set `root` to the main vault for First implementation or Modification, or to the verified prepared worktree for a dependent Bug fix. Pass `decision` from the router, selected `ticket` text, `plan_path` for a new plan, exact implementation `files`, and `sections` mapping exact note paths to arrays of heading paths. For example, a heading path is `["Specification", "Acceptance"]`. Pass the effective role `settings` and relevant `context`. The helper requests a read-only planner proposal and checks and writes the resulting documents.*

 *Use the returned `response` in the current ticket. A Ready plan remains ready until execution starts. A returned `execute` stage includes validated `tasks` to give to the orchestrator. On a later explicit execution request, route using the plan's internal Ready status, then invoke the helper with the same exact authorized implementation paths to validate its current task table. The frontmatter Status remains user-owned.*
